# Production overlay for firmware/phase3-tailscale (applied after
# sdkconfig.defaults, before sdkconfig.secrets):  tm build --prod
#
# - No test hooks: WIFI_DOWN on the echo port would let any tailnet peer the
#   ACL admits take the board offline.
# - Warnings only in the logs (MicroLink's own INFO logs cost ~20 KB of flash
#   and leak peer names / IPs to anyone on the serial port). METRIC lines are
#   printf and stay.
#
# NOT set here, on purpose: flash encryption and NVS encryption. Enabling them
# burns eFuses on first boot, which cannot be undone, and this board
# (ESP32-D0WD rev 1.0) only has Secure Boot V1. Do it deliberately on the
# production hardware, following ESP-IDF's flash-encryption guide
# (docs/03 section 10).
CONFIG_TM_TEST_HOOKS=n
CONFIG_LOG_DEFAULT_LEVEL_WARN=y
CONFIG_ML_LOG_LEVEL_WARN=y
